  "plain": "Dennis Asberg, a treasure hunter, helped find the Baltic Sea anomaly, an oddly shaped object on the seabed between Sweden and Finland. He says that from about 2011, while his team was at the site, their radar showed something about 150 meters away even though nothing was there, a moment he connects with a colleague, Peter Lindberg. To him, it hints that something unseen was watching the site."
